{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"2223db08c03d7e3d20fe181f9e244cd59282bfea3aebca806f6995d8c366cd06","digest":{"component_or_area":"LLM provider mapping and resolution","key_entities":["src/rebar/llm/config.py","_PROVIDER_PREFIXES","infer_provider","google_genai","google","_pydantic_ai_known_providers","ProviderSession","KNOWN_PROVIDER_NAMES","anthropic_model._pai_model","model_classes._resolve_target","_PAI_PROVIDER_PREFIX","tests/unit/test_provider_qualifier.py","tests/interfaces/store/test_llm_framework.py"],"problem_keywords":["provider inference","gemini model id","provider resolution","pydantic-ai compatibility","model configuration"],"propositions":["Bare gemini-* model ids map through infer_provider to 'google_genai', a provider name unknown to both pydantic-ai and rebar's ProviderSession, causing LLMConfigError at call time","The defect manifests in model_classes._resolve_target (model-class/ladder path) but not in anthropic_model._pai_model (bare cfg.model path) due to a private _PAI_PROVIDER_PREFIX translation table","Changing _PROVIDER_PREFIXES to map gemini -> 'google' (pydantic-ai's canonical Gemini Developer API name) makes bare gemini-* ids resolvable without breaking existing back-compat shims","All inferred provider names must belong to either _pydantic_ai_known_providers() or ProviderSession._builders to prevent future prefix additions from reintroducing the same defect class"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787624816212233001,"uuid":"2cbc0486-f38c-4336-9d17-bd7af5d1cc61"}